cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "Wuhan Logs"
abstract: >-
  A source-based log of how evidence about the origins of COVID-19 reached
  the public: disclosure, research oversight and public communication,
  tracked over time. It contains a chronology, an evidence register of
  claims with their sources and limits, an annotated source register,
  accountability dossiers, a reusable disclosure control framework and
  draft proposals. It takes no position on whether the pandemic began
  through animal spillover or a research-related incident. The initial
  edition was AI-assisted and is being verified against its sources.
authors:
  - family-names: "de Jong"
    given-names: "Michiel"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/michielbdejong/wuhan-logs"
version: "2026-11-17"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
keywords:
  - COVID-19
  - SARS-CoV-2
  - pandemic origins
  - disclosure
  - research oversight
  - transparency
  - accountability
  - evidence register
